     "<p dir=\"ltr\"><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"></p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">On Fri, Aug 21, 2015, 2:34 PM arnaud gaboury &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">arnaud....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\">I downloaded and uncompressed the RRO package from Revolutionanalytics. Running the following command inside the directory:<br></p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">-------------------------------</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"># dnf -y --nogpgcheck install RRO-3.2.1-el7.x86_64.rpm   </p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Last metadata expiration check performed 0:46:27 ago on Fri Aug 21 13:40:11 2015.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Error: nothing provides libicui18n.so.50()(64bit) needed by RRO-3.2.1-3.2.1-1.el7.centos.x86_64</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">(try to add &#39;--allowerasing&#39; to command line to replace conflicting packages)</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">----------------------------<br></p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The icu package is in fact installing<b> libicui18n.so.54</b>. Before I go further on the install, please tell me if it possible to use thi newer version of icu or shall I downgrade ?<br></p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Thank you for </p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">hint</p>\r\n"
    ],
